---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import BuildMarker from '../../components/BuildMarker.astro';
import { buildInfo } from '../../generated/build-info.mjs';
import { listArticles } from '../../lib/articles.mjs';

const allArticles = await listArticles();
---

<Layout
  title="About — Field Notes"
  description="How the Field Notes static library is built, verified and deployed."
  active="about"
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Small, static, verifiable.</h1>
    <p>
      Field Notes is a deliberately small knowledge base that exercises the whole static-site
      toolchain: content collections, nested routes, local assets and a fully client-side search.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <p>
      {allArticles.length} articles live in an Astro content collection
      (<code>src/content/articles/</code>) with a typed schema in
      <code>src/content.config.ts</code>. The production build pre-renders every route to plain
      HTML under <code>dist/</code>:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>/</code> — home with hero, categories and recent notes</li>
      <li><code>/library/</code> — search & browse all notes (embedded client search)</li>
      <li><code>/library/articles/[slug]/</code> — each article detail page</li>
      <li><code>/library/categories/</code> and <code>/library/categories/[name]/</code> — nested category browsing</li>
      <li><code>/about/</code> — this page</li>
      <li><code>/404</code> — styled not-found page</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How search works</h2>
    <p>
      The article index is embedded in the library page at build time. The matcher lives in
      <code>src/lib/search.mjs</code> — a pure, dependency-free module that scores title, tag,
      category, description and body text. It runs in the browser after load and is covered by
      the same unit tests. A dedicated empty state is shown when nothing matches.
    </p>

    <h2>Install, build and run</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Command</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>npm ci</code></td><td>Reproducible install from the lockfile</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>npm run dev</code></td><td>Dev server on 127.0.0.1:4321</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>npm run build</code></td><td>Write the static site to <code>dist/</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>npm run preview</code></td><td>Serve built <code>dist/</code> on 127.0.0.1:4321</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>npm run check</code></td><td><code>astro check</code> type checks</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>npm test</code></td><td>Unit tests + end-to-end smoke suite</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Runtime and environment</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Runtime: Node.js 22.12+ (pinned via <code>engines</code>), npm with a committed <code>package-lock.json</code></li>
      <li>Bind: <code>127.0.0.1</code> (host can be overridden with <code>--host</code>)</li>
      <li>Port: <code>4321</code> for dev/preview (override with <code>--port</code> or <code>PORT</code>)</li>
      <li>Environment: no secrets. Copy <code>.env.example</code> if you want to set optional values.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Health and persistence</h2>
    <p>
      This is a static site — there is no database, backend or worker process, so traditional
      liveness/readiness probes and restart persistence checks do not apply. <code>/healthz.txt</code>
      is an honest static availability marker only, and deployment status is tracked in
      <code>VERIFICATION.md</code>, not inferred from a static file.
    </p>

    <h2>Build marker</h2>
    <p>
      Every page footer shows the exact revision this build came from (see below), generated by
      <code>scripts/build-info.mjs</code> at build time and recreated on every build.
    </p>

    <p class="marker-row"><BuildMarker /></p>
    <p class="sub">commit full: <code>{buildInfo.commitFull || 'development'}</code></p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .page-header h1 {
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .page-header p:not(.eyebrow) {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .marker-row {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .sub {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
</style>